course: dictionary
lesson: 4716
title: Context in nature words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word you do not know can still make sense when you read the words around it. In «a bird called the hoopoe brings him news», the word bird tells you a hoopoe is an animal, not a person or a place.
explain: Descriptions give clues too. «Hoopoe chicks squirt smelly poo and a nasty oil at intruders» shows the chicks defend themselves. Intruders are unwanted visitors, so the chicks are protecting their nest from danger.
explain: Look at «a hoopoe's crest». The 's shows the crest belongs to the hoopoe, so it is part of its head. Check by swapping in your meaning: «a bird's head feathers» still makes sense, so you have understood it.
fact: A hoopoe is a bird found in Africa, Europe and Asia.
fact: A hoopoe has pinkish-brown feathers and black-and-white striped wings.
fact: Its crest is a big tuft of feathers on its head that opens out like a fan.
fact: The hoopoe's call sounds like oop-oop-oop.
fact: The hoopoe is the national bird of Israel.
exercise: «Hoopoe chicks squirt smelly poo and a nasty oil at intruders.» What do the chicks squirt at intruders? | *Smelly poo and a nasty oil | Bright red paint | Clean water from a pond | Seeds and crumbs
exercise: What sound does a hoopoe's call make? | Tweet-tweet-tweet | Moo-moo-moo | Quack-quack-quack | *Oop-oop-oop
exercise: A hoopoe's crest looks like a big what on its head? | A nest | A hat | *A fan | A cloud
test: Which part of a hoopoe is black and white striped? | Its beak | Its tail feathers | Its feet | *Its wings
test: In the old tale, what does the hoopoe bring to Solomon? | A golden crown | Bread and water | *News | A song about the sun
exam: In «a big crest like a fan on its head», what does crest mean? | *A tuft of feathers on the head | A pool of water | A long, thin beak | A striped wing
